# 5. Page Customisation

Create a dedicated Page Settings panel.

Users must be able to modify the following settings.

## A. Page Orientation

Only two options:

- Portrait.
- Landscape.

## B. Page Size

A4 only.

Use actual A4 proportions:

- Portrait: 210 × 297 mm.
- Landscape: 297 × 210 mm.

Do not introduce other paper sizes.

## C. Page Colour

Provide a selection of monochromatic paper colours:

- Pure white.
- Off-white.
- Light grey.
- Medium grey.
- Dark charcoal.
- Black.

Ensure that template contrast automatically adjusts according to the selected page colour.

For example, dark templates should not become invisible on dark paper.

## D. Page Template

Provide the following built-in templates:

### Lined

- Lined (standard).
- Lined (narrow).
- Lined (wide).

### Grid

- Grid (standard).
- Grid (narrow).
- Grid (wide).

### Dot

- Dot (standard).
- Dot (narrow).
- Dot (wide).

### Other

- Oxford.

### Custom

An option labelled "Add Your Own".

Users should be able to upload:

- PNG files.
- PDF files.

The application should convert imported PDF template pages into suitable background assets.

For a multipage PDF, allow the user to choose which PDF page to use as the template.

Provide a preview before applying the imported template.

Allow the user to remove or replace custom templates.

Imported templates should be stored locally and remain available after restarting the application.

### Template Rendering Architecture

This requires special attention because the templates must work in all three document formats.

Do NOT generate a giant background image.

Instead:

- Render built-in templates procedurally using CSS, SVG or canvas patterns.
- Use consistent mathematical spacing.
- Reuse the same rendering implementation across all formats.
- Repeat the pattern across successive A4 pages.
- In Infinite Canvas mode, repeat the template seamlessly across the world coordinate system.
- Ensure that the pattern does not visibly jump or reset when zooming or panning.
- Render custom PDF/PNG templates as repeating page-sized background assets.

Suggested initial spacing values:

| Template | Standard | Narrow | Wide |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Lined | 7 mm | 5 mm | 9 mm |
| Grid | 5 mm | 3 mm | 8 mm |
| Dot | 5 mm | 3 mm | 8 mm |

Oxford paper should use standard horizontal ruling with a vertical margin line.

These values can be refined later.

All templates must remain crisp and appropriately scaled at different zoom levels.

