# 6. Drawing and Handwriting System

The drawing experience should be heavily inspired by Samsung Notes.

The vertical toolbar should contain dedicated drawing tools.

Clicking an icon should open a floating settings panel associated with that tool.

Only one tool popup should be open at a time.

Clicking elsewhere, clicking another tool or pressing Escape should close the existing popup.

The popup should not remain permanently attached to the screen.

## A. Pen Tool

Clicking the pen icon should open a floating panel similar to the first supplied screenshot.

The panel should contain:

### Pen Presets

Provide five distinct pen types:

1. Fountain pen.
2. Ballpoint pen.
3. Marker.
4. Pencil.
5. Brush pen.

Each should have its own stroke characteristics.

Examples:

- Fountain pen: pressure-sensitive strokes with a tapered, ink-like appearance.
- Ballpoint: consistent, precise strokes.
- Marker: thicker, smooth strokes.
- Pencil: textured-looking strokes.
- Brush: variable-width strokes depending on pressure and movement.

Allow users to select a pen preset.

### Stroke Width

Provide:

- Minus button.
- Adjustable slider.
- Current numerical width.
- Plus button.

Changing the slider should immediately affect the selected pen.

Stroke widths should be adjustable over a practical range.

Support pressure-sensitive stylus input where available.

### Straighten Lines

Include a toggle labelled:

"Straighten lines"

When enabled, recognise approximately straight strokes and smooth or correct them into straight lines.

This should not interfere with normal handwriting unnecessarily.

### Colour Selection

Provide a row of recent colours and quick-access swatches.

The default swatches should use white, black and shades of grey.

Allow custom colour selection for actual written content, while keeping the colour-picker interface itself monochromatic.

Include:

- Eyedropper.
- Custom colour picker.
- Recent colours.
- Saved pen presets/favourites.

### Popup Controls

Include:

- Save/favourite preset.
- Expand/collapse option.
- Close button.

Allow the user to customise and retain their preferred pen configurations.

## B. Highlighter

The highlighter should have its own popup.

Include:

- Multiple highlighter styles.
- Stroke-width adjustment.
- Colour selection.
- Opacity adjustment.
- Straight-line correction where appropriate.

Highlighter strokes should render beneath or appropriately blend with handwriting rather than obscuring it.

## C. Eraser

Provide:

- Stroke eraser.
- Area eraser.

The stroke eraser should remove the selected stroke.

The area eraser should remove only the intersecting portions of strokes and other supported drawing elements, rather than deleting an entire large stroke unnecessarily.

Provide adjustable eraser size.

## D. Lasso Selection

Implement a freeform selection tool.

Users should be able to draw a selection boundary around existing content.

The selection should support:

- Move.
- Resize.
- Rotate.
- Copy.
- Cut.
- Paste.
- Duplicate.
- Delete.

It should recognise and select supported ink strokes and shapes.

Provide a clearly visible selection boundary and transformation handles.

## E. Shapes and Straight-Line Tool

Provide common drawing shapes:

- Straight line.
- Arrow.
- Rectangle.
- Rounded rectangle.
- Circle/ellipse.
- Triangle.
- Polygon.

Allow users to select stroke width and colour.

Support shape recognition where practical.

For example, approximately circular handwriting should be convertible into a clean circle when shape recognition is enabled.

