# 7. Popup and Tool Interaction Behaviour

This is an important part of recreating the usability of the reference interface.

Every toolbar tool must have predictable behaviour.

Rules:

1. Clicking a tool selects it.
2. Clicking its settings icon or selected tool again should open or close its configuration popup.
3. Clicking a different tool closes the previous popup.
4. Clicking outside a popup closes it.
5. Pressing Escape closes it.
6. Only one popup can be open at a time.
7. Popups should appear near the relevant toolbar icon.
8. Popups must remain within the visible application area.
9. Popup interactions should not accidentally draw on the canvas.
10. Tool selection and tool configuration must remain separate states.

Do not create multiple permanently visible side panels for individual tools.

The interface should remain clean.

