# 8. Keyboard and Rich-Text Editor

The keyboard tool is a major part of One Book.

It must not behave like a conventional floating text box.

When the keyboard icon is clicked, activate a proper document-style rich-text editor.

The writing experience should resemble Google Docs or Microsoft Word.

### Fundamental behaviour

- The cursor should start at the top-left content margin when the document is empty.
- Users should be able to type continuously.
- Text should automatically wrap.
- Text should flow naturally into subsequent pages.
- Users should never have to manually resize text boxes.
- Users should not have to manually create a new page when text reaches the bottom of an existing page.
- The editor should support normal keyboard shortcuts.
- Text content should coexist with the drawing and handwriting system.

Use a single continuous rich-text document model, not a collection of unrelated textarea elements.

The editor should behave as a unified document that can be visually presented through the three page formats.

### Rich-Text Toolbar

When keyboard mode is active, show an appropriate text-formatting toolbar.

Include:

**Basic formatting**
- Font family.
- Font size.
- Bold.
- Italic.
- Underline.
- Strikethrough.
- Text colour.
- Text highlight.

**Paragraph formatting**
- Left alignment.
- Centre alignment.
- Right alignment.
- Justification.
- Bulleted lists.
- Numbered lists.
- Indentation.
- Line spacing.

**Advanced formatting**
- Heading levels.
- Hyperlinks.
- Superscript.
- Subscript.
- Undo.
- Redo.

### Fonts

Provide an initial font library containing:

- Lora.
- Cormorant Garamond.
- Libre Baskerville.
- Georgia.
- Times New Roman.
- Arial.
- Courier New.
- IBM Plex Mono.

Make the default document font Lora.

Allow font sizes to be changed easily.

### Text Layout

Use automatic pagination.

Text must reflow properly when:

- Page orientation changes.
- Page format changes.
- Page margins change.
- Font size changes.
- Font family changes.

Avoid implementing each page as an independent editor.

Maintain one underlying rich-text document and implement a pagination/layout system that places content into the visible page representation.

In particular, preserve the cursor position, text selection and editing state when pagination is recalculated.

