# 11. System Architecture

Use a modular architecture rather than putting the entire application inside one React component.

## Recommended Technology Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Language | TypeScript |
| UI framework | React |
| Build system | Vite |
| Styling | CSS Modules or structured CSS |
| Application state | Zustand |
| Rich-text editor | Tiptap / ProseMirror |
| Drawing engine | HTML Canvas with a vector-based stroke model |
| Stroke rendering | Perfect Freehand |
| PDF processing | PDF.js |
| Persistent storage | IndexedDB using Dexie |
| Icons | Lucide |
| Runtime validation | Zod |
| Unit testing | Vitest |
| Browser testing | Playwright |

Use strict TypeScript configuration.

Avoid unnecessary dependencies and avoid using `any` as a substitute for proper type definitions.

## Architecture Overview

Organise the application into six logical systems.

### 1. Application Shell

Responsible for:
- Navigation.
- Toolbars.
- Popups.
- Settings.
- Notebook library.
- Application layout.

### 2. Document Engine

Responsible for:
- Document structure.
- Document metadata.
- Page settings.
- Document format.
- Orientation.
- Page generation.
- Content coordinates.

### 3. Rendering Engine

Responsible for:
- Page surfaces.
- Background templates.
- Ink rendering.
- Shape rendering.
- Text presentation.
- Canvas zooming.
- Canvas panning.
- Clipping and visibility.

### 4. Input Engine

Responsible for:
- Mouse input.
- Stylus input.
- Touch input.
- Pen tools.
- Eraser.
- Lasso.
- Shape recognition.
- Gesture handling.

### 5. Editing Engine

Responsible for:
- Tiptap rich-text editing.
- Text pagination.
- Document selection.
- Undo and redo.
- Clipboard operations.

### 6. Storage Engine

Responsible for:
- IndexedDB.
- Automatic saving.
- Document loading.
- Asset storage.
- Export.
- Import.
- Data validation.

These systems should communicate through well-defined TypeScript interfaces.

